        <briefdescription>
<para>Default constructor. Constructs an iterator pointing to <computeroutput>nullptr</computeroutput>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The default constructor for <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1utils_1_1doubly__list__iterator" kindref="compound">doubly_list_iterator</ref></computeroutput> initialises the iterator to a null state, meaning it does not point to any node in the list. This is typically used to create an &quot;end&quot; iterator or to initialise an iterator variable before assigning it to a valid node.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>The internal node pointer is value-initialised (set to <computeroutput>nullptr</computeroutput>), ensuring that the iterator is safe to use in comparisons and will not dereference an invalid address. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
