This constructor creates a <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1utils_1_1doubly__list__iterator" kindref="compound">doubly_list_iterator</ref></computeroutput> that points to the specified node. The internal node pointer is set to the provided node address, allowing the iterator to traverse the list starting from that node. This constructor is typically used to initialise an iterator to a specific position within the list, such as the beginning or end. </para>
