    <briefdescription>
<para>A class template for a doubly linked list iterator. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Type of object returned by the iterator. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>N</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Type of intrusive node. Must have the public members <bold>previous</bold> &amp; <bold>next</bold>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>U</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Type stored in the list, derived from T.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
This iterator provides an interface similar to <computeroutput>std::list::iterator</computeroutput> for traversing a doubly linked list. It supports bidirectional iteration and access to the underlying node and value. In a typical doubly linked list, all types are <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1utils_1_1doubly__list__links" kindref="compound">doubly_list_links</ref></computeroutput>. </para>
